###########################
#  Main text

BEGIN_TEXT
Let \( F:\mathbb{R}^3 \to \mathbb{R}^3 \) and \( G : \mathbb{R}^3 \to \mathbb{R}^3 \) be a \( C^2 \) vector fields with \( F = (F_1,F_2,F_3) \) and \( G = (G_1,G_2,G_3) \).  Let \( f : \mathbb{R}^3 \to \mathbb{R} \) be a \( C^2 \) scalar function. Which statements are true, false, or nonsense? $BR $BR


1. \( \text{div}(F) = \partial_1 F_1 + \partial_2 F_2 + \partial_3 F_3 \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio1->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
2. \( \text{div}(F) = \nabla \cdot F \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio2->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
3. \( \text{div}( \nabla f) = 0 \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio3->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
4. \( \text{div}( \nabla f) = \partial_1^2 f + \partial_2^2 f + \partial_3^2 f \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio4->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
5. \( \text{div}( \nabla F) = \nabla \cdot \nabla F \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio5->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
6. \( \nabla (\text{div}(F) ) = F \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio6->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
7. \( \nabla(fg) = f \nabla g + g \nabla f \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio7->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_TEXT
8. \( \text{div}(FG) = \text{div}(F) G + F \text{div}(G) \)
END_TEXT

BEGIN_PGML
[@ $radio8->buttons() @]*
END_PGML

############################
